  <static seed="1930" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/IntegerAndSquareRoot/identifySquareNumbers50.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p>Do not use a calculator.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{81} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{8100} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{810000} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>        9</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>       90</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>      900</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>First, recognize that <m>81</m> is a square number. Since <m>9\cdot9=81</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{81}=9</m>.</p>
<p>Next, since <m>90\cdot90=8100</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{8100}=90</m>.</p>
<p>Finally, since <m>900\cdot900=810000</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{810000}=900</m>.</p>
</solution>
